<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42194" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">să_crĭfĭcus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to a sacrificing</i>, <i>sacrificial</i> (<b>poet.</b>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">not ante-Aug.): securis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 12, 249</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dies,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 13, 590</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ritus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					ib. 15, 483</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">arae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Val.
					Fl. 8, 243</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vestis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil. 3,
					27</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">os,</span>”
				<i>of those sacrificing</i>, <i>praying</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. F.
					1, 130</span></i>
			: Ancus, <i>mindful of sacrifices</i> or <i>of religion</i> in gen., <i><span class="en">id. ib. 6,
				803</span></i>; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Numa,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Luc.
					9, 478</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">jugum,</span>”
				<i>where human sacrifices were offered</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Val.
					Fl. 4, 110</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">preces,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen.
					Med. 38</span></i>
			: rex, v. rex, I.</div>
